[Lemma lem:I:minus:beta:larger of arXiv:2607.04047, 'Top Singular Value in Sum-Products of Random Matrices'] Assume $x_0 = \Theta(1)$ and $K=\Theta((\log m)^{1/4})$. For $\beta > x_0$, we have that conditioning on $A_\epsilon$ with $\epsilon \in (0,1)$,
\begin{align*}
    \Big| 
        \mfrac{ \log I_-}{x_0 \beta \log m - \frac{x_0^2}{2} \log m  } 
        \,-\, 
        1
    \Big|
    \;=&\;
    O\Big( 
        \mfrac{\epsilon}{(1-\epsilon)\log m}
        +
        \mfrac{1}{(\log m)^{1/4}}
    \Big)
    \;.
\end{align*}

