[Lemma 13 of arXiv:2607.11608, '2607.11608'] Let  $\mu$ as in \eqref{mu_def}.  Then, for every $K\in \R$ and $\eps>0$,
\begin{equation*}
\mu\bigg(\int_{\R^d}:\!|\P_{N}u|^2\!:dx \in [K-\eps,K+\eps]\bigg)\les \eps,
\end{equation*}
where the implicit constant is independent of $K$ and $\eps$. 
In particular, the same holds true for $\int_{\R^d}:\!|u|^2\!:dx=\lim_{N\to +\infty}\int_{\R^d}:\!|\P_{N}u|^2\!: dx$. (Proof in the paper; no proof environment follows the statement in the TeX.)

[Lemma lem:wcutoff of arXiv:2608.23135, 'Graph distance and effective resistance of the random walk trace in four and five dimensio'] For fixed $\varepsilon$ and $\delta$,
\begin{equation*}

   \mathbb{P}(L_{\mathrm{RW}}\ne L_{\mathrm{RW}}^R)
   \le \frac{C\delta^{-1}\varepsilon^{-1}}{R}+o_n(1).
\end{equation*}

