{"artifact_digest":"sha256:d99d743136566242455151b47c0efadf5b464b174b41492f1d454578446bb779","artifact_path":"objects/sha256/d9/d99d743136566242455151b47c0efadf5b464b174b41492f1d454578446bb779.md","bundle_digest":"sha256:1ae1b1bff39ea6a343887371db05c86fa4e43220103b7df42f69d006fc9ae469","bundle_entry_key":"2608-23765-theorem-18-one-step-local-contraction","bundle_id":"population.tex-extract-s0_036","claim_kind":"theorem","conditions":[],"domain":"probability theory","draft":"tex-extract-v2-20260907/bundle_s0_036.json","evidence_ids":[],"logical_id":"math:harvest.arxiv.mathematics:arxiv-2608-23765-proposition-18-one-step-local-contraction","overlay_schema_version":1,"proof_text":"Paper's own proof, opening: The proof of this proposition is structurally similar to the proof of (prop:p1:linearrate of the paper).
Again, we define $ \mathbf{N}^{(k)} := \mathbf{X}_\star - \mathbf{X}^{(k)} $.
By the monotonicity of $\varepsilon \mapsto \mathcal{J}_{\varepsilon}(\mathbf{X}^{(k+1)})$, the majorization property for $q$-power mean weights with $q\ge -1$, and the optimality of $\mathbf{X}^{(k+1)}$ in (eq:IRLS:step_1 of the paper), for any $t \in \mathbb{R}$ we have that
\begin{equation}
\mathcal{J}_{\varepsilon_{k+1}}(\mathbf{X}^{(k+1)}) \leq Q_{\varepsilon_k} (\mathbf{X}^{(k+1)} \mid \mathbf{X}^{(k)}) \leq Q_{\varepsilon_k}(\mathbf{X}^{(k)}+t \mathbf{N}^{(k)} \mid ...","release_manifest_digest":"sha256:1aaa301685015c36cc65d3cfda32f0139f7ebb306319d9c6b2fa0f6c03d32026","revision_digest":"sha256:ca2761af149e504283f0062f0578891fd8564cebf3c88c668420b9c288a486d7","source_id":"arxiv:2608.23765","source_revision":"tex-as-downloaded-2026-09-08","statement_fidelity_reviewed":false,"supersedes":[],"trust_class":"curated_secondary","truth_status":"unverified"}

