[Theorem 70 of arXiv:2605.03236, 'Stochastic It\^o Equations and Parabolic Second-Order Equations with singular Drift'] Let $\tau=0$, $\cA=\Omega$, so that
\eqref{10.16.1} becomes
\begin{equation}

E \int_{0}^{\infty}e^{- \lambda s}
f(s,x_{ s} ) \,ds =\int_{\bR^{d+1}}f(t,x)G_{\Omega}(t,x)\,dxdt,
\end{equation}
where $G_{\Omega}(t,x)$ is nonrandom. 
Then for any $\varepsilon\in(0,\rho^{2}_{b})$
\begin{equation}

\int_{C_{\rho_{b}}\setminus\{t<\varepsilon\}}G^{-\mu}_{\Omega}(t,x)\,
dxdt\leq N(\varepsilon,d,\delta,\rho_{b},\lambda)<\infty,
\end{equation}
where $\mu>0$ is taken from
Corollary \ref{corollary 10.1,1}. (Proof in the paper; no proof environment follows the statement in the TeX.)

[Lemma lem4new of arXiv:2411.04238, 'Holomorphic jump-diffusions'] Fix $T >0$,  $\lambda=(\lambda_k)_{k \in \mathbb{N}_0}$, and  $\mu\in \mathcal B$ such that
$$(\lambda_0\mu_0,\lambda_1\mu_1,\lambda_2\mu_2,\ldots)\in \mathcal{S}^*.$$
Assume that
$$\mathcal A (\lambda_k\frac{(\cdot)^k}{k!})(x)=\sum_{j=0}^\infty \beta_{kj}(\lambda_j\frac{x^j}{j!}-\lambda_k\frac{x^k}{k!})+\beta_k\lambda_k\frac {x^k}{k!}$$
for some $\beta_{kj}\in \mathbb R_+$ and $\beta_k\in \mathbb R$ such that $\sup_{k\geq 0}\beta_k^+<\infty$ and $\lim_{j\to\infty}\beta_{kj}=0$ for each $k\in \mathbb{N}_0$. 
If for all $x\in (-\epsilon,1+\epsilon)$ the sequence 
\begin{equation}
\Big(\lambda_k\frac{x^k}{k!},\sum_{j=0}^\infty \beta_{kj}(\lambda_j\frac{x^j}{j!}-\lambda_k\frac{x^k}{k!})\Big)_{k\in\mathbb{N}_0}
\end{equation}
lies in the bounded pointwise closure of 
\begin{equation*}
\Big\{\Big(\mathbf{a}_k,\sum_{j=0}^\infty \beta_{kj}(\mathbf{a}_j-\mathbf{a}_k)\Big)_{k\in \mathbb{N}_0}\colon \mathbf{a}=(\mathbf{a}_k)_{k=0}^N,\quad N\in \mathbb{N}\Big\},
\end{equation*}
then the linear ODE given by (equation eq:ODE sequence space holomorphic of the paper) admits a solution $({\bf c}(t))_{t\in[0,T]}$ satisfying (equation eq: ODE pointwise of the paper) for each $x\in S$ of the form  ${\bf c}_k(t)=\lambda_k\mu_k(t)$ for some $\mu_k(t)\geq0$. If $\beta_k\leq 0$ for each $k$, then  $\sum_{k=0}^\infty\mu_k(t)\leq \sum_{k=0}^\infty\mu_k$.

[Theorem 9 (The $m$th-order Santal\'o inequality on $\R^n$) of arXiv:2609.01460, 'On cost-induced Santal\'o-type inequalities \\ in Polish measure spaces'] Fix $Q\in\conbodo[m].$ Let $K\subset \R^n$ be a compact set of positive volume such that $K$ or $K^\circ$ has center of mass at the origin. Then,
  \begin{equation}
  \Vol(K^{\star,Q})\vol(K)^m \leq \vol(\B)^m \Vol((B_2^n)^{\star,Q}).

\end{equation}
There is equality if and only if $K=E$ for some centered ellipsoid $E\subset\R^n$ up to removal of null sets. (Proof in the paper; no proof environment follows the statement in the TeX.)

