[Lemma lem:Push-TASEP-WF of arXiv:2608.02772, 'Non-Abelian Hirota-Miwa Equations for the KPZ Universality Class'] The product-graph wave functions satisfy the
semi-discrete linear problem
(equation eq:sc-linear-1 of the paper)--(equation eq:sc-linear-j of the paper)
and its adjoint
(equation eq:sc-adjoint-1 of the paper)--(equation eq:sc-adjoint-j of the paper)
with the shifts and edge weights above.
Explicitly:
\begin{align}
\partial_t \Psi^{t,\mathbf{a},\mathbf{n}}
&= 2\bigl(\Psi^{t,\mathbf{a}+\mathbf{1},\mathbf{n}}
   - \Psi^{t,\mathbf{a},\mathbf{n}}\bigr),
 \\
