body:
[Thm dBM of arXiv:2411.14090, '{\bf Exponential Ergodicity in $\W_1$ for SDEs with Distribution Dependent Noise and Parti'] Suppose that {\bf(A2)} holds with
\begin{equation}
(K_1+L_b)\gamma^{-2}\leq \frac{K_1}{2(K_1+L_b)}.

\end{equation}
Then there exists a constant $\delta_0>0$ such that when $\kappa<\delta_0$, (equation Langevin of the paper) has a unique invariant probability measure $\mu^\ast\in\mathbb P_1(\mathbb R^{2d})$ and there exist constants $c,\lambda>0$ such that
\begin{equation*}
  \mathbb W_1(P_t^*\eta, \mu^\ast)\leq c
   \text{\rm{e}}^{-\lambda t}
  \mathbb W_1(\eta, \mu^\ast),\quad \eta\in\mathscr P_1(\mathbb R^{2d}),\, t\geq 0.
\end{equation*} (Proof in the paper; no proof environment follows the statement in the TeX.)

