[Theorem 3 of arXiv:2606.06489, 'The Missing Central Limit Theorems for Local Functionals of Berry's Random Wave Model'] As $R\to\infty$, the \emph{defect} or \emph{signed volume} of Berry's model,
    \begin{equation*}
    D(R)=|\set{x\in B_R: u_1(x)>0}|-|\set{x\in B_R: u_1(x)<0}|,
    \quad R>0,    
    \end{equation*}
    satisfies $\var D(R)\sim C R^d$, $C>0$, and $\frac{D(R)}{\sqrt{\var D(R)}}$ converges in 1-Wasserstein distance to a standard Gaussian random variable as $\R\to\infty$. (Proof in the paper; no proof environment follows the statement in the TeX.)

