[Lemma L_strTWB of arXiv:2510.26724, 'Sharp Fuss-Catalan thresholds in graph bootstrap percolation'] Let $T$ be a TWG and $S\subsetneq T$ a partial TWG. Then, 
\begin{enumerate}
\item $\mathcal E(S)\geqslant 0$, with equality 
if and only $S$ is obtained from $T$ 
by removing one of its branches; 
\item $\mathcal D(S,T)\leqslant c\mathcal E(S)+2$; and 
\item $\mathcal T(S)\leqslant c\mathcal E(S)$, 
\end{enumerate}
for some constant $c$ depending only on $r$. (Proof in the paper; no proof environment follows the statement in the TeX.)

[Proposition 7 (Pointwise finite-particle convergence to the target in KSD) of arXiv:2608.28827, 'Quantitative Target Convergence and Uniform-in-Time\\ Propagation of Chaos for Langevin-Re'] Under Assumptions~\ref{ass:core-target} and \ref{ass:ksd-kernel},
\begin{align}
    \E\KSD(\mu_t^N\|\pi)
    &\le C\left(\int(1+\|y\|)^2\pi(dy)\right)^{1/2}
       \left(\frac{2H_N(t)}{\alpha N}\right)^{1/2}
       +\frac1{\sqrt N}
        \left(\int\|\xi_\pi(y)\|_{\mathcal H^d}^2\pi(dy)\right)^{1/2}
       \\
    &\le C e^{-\varepsilon\alpha t}+\frac{C}{\sqrt N}.

\end{align}

