[Lemma LemGeoOneStep of arXiv:2608.28949, 'The information geometry of product-reference discrete diffusion: Interaction growth compl'] For any $0 < a < b < 1$, the one-step KL error satisfies the bound
\begin{align}

  \Gamma_{\scaleto{\operatorname{prod}}{5pt}}(a, b) & \leq 2 \left\{ \frac{\ensuremath{\psi}(b)}{\ensuremath{\psi}(a)} - 1 \right\}
  \mathsf{G}(a, b),
\end{align}
where $\ensuremath{\psi}(r) \coloneqq r/(1 - r)$. (Proof in the paper; no proof environment follows the statement in the TeX.)

[Proposition 47 (Square-root promotion) of arXiv:2608.12492, 'Weak Limits of Wiener Chaos: Primitive--Fock Classification and Hilbert--Stein Extraction'] Suppose
\[
 0\le N_q\le MR^2\Id,
 \qquad
 E_q=R_q^*N_qR_q,
\]
and let $L$ be a top eigenspace of $E_q$, with eigenvalue $\lambda>0$.  Set
\begin{equation}
 V_q^{1/2}=\Ran(N_q^{1/2}R_qL).

\end{equation}
Then, for every unit $c\in L$,
\begin{equation}
 \norm{P_{V_q^{1/2}}R_qc}^2
 \ge\frac{\lambda}{MR^2},
 \qquad
 \norm{N_q^{1/2}R_qc}^2=\lambda.

\end{equation}
Moreover
\begin{equation}
 \ip{N_q^{1/2}R_qc}{N_q^{1/2}R_qc'}
 =\ip{R_qc}{N_qR_qc'},

\end{equation}
which is a four-source Gram.

