Since we have 

\begin{gather}

\tilde{z}'(t)-\varepsilon \Delta_N \tilde{z}(t)=\tilde{v}'(t) \quad \text{in} \quad L^2(\Omega),\quad \text{a.e.}~t \in (0,T),\\

\tilde{z}(0)=z_0 \quad \text{in} \quad L^2(\Omega),
\end{gather}

we take the inner product in both sides of \eqref{Equation-3-9} in $L^2(\Omega)$ by $\tilde{z}'(t)$ and obtain

