[Definition def:stopping_times of arXiv:2603.24803, 'Critical Spectral Invariants in Random Walks with Geometric Resetting'] Define the following random times:

\begin{align*}
&\tau_0 := \inf\{\, n \ge 1 :X_n = 0 \,\}, \text{(first passage to $0$),} \\[4pt]\\
&\tau_a:= \inf\{\, n \ge 1 :X_n = a \,\}, \text{(first passage to $a$),} \\[4pt]\\
&\tau := \min\{\tau_0, \tau_a\}, \text{(first exit from $(0,a)$).}
\end{align*}

[Lem 10 (All good) of arXiv:2606.27035, 'R\'emy's diffusion on Brownian trees'] The following events occur with a probability tending to $1$ as $n \to \infty$:
\begin{enumerate}
\item $T_0^{\, \bullet}, \ldots, T_n^{\, \bullet}$ are all $n$-good when $T_0^{\, \bullet}$ is a single vertex;
\item $T_0^{\, \bullet}, \ldots, T_{\Resamp-1}^{\, \bullet}$ are all $\max(n,\Resamp)$-good when $T_0^{\, \bullet}=(t,x)$ is $n$-good.
\item $T_{\Resamp}$ is $\max(n,\Resamp)$-good when the non-marked tree $T_0$ is $n$-good.
\end{enumerate}

