body:
[Lemma 20 (Binomial resolvents) of arXiv:2608.25706, 'Fast rates in Bayesian online learning with approximate posteriors'] \label[lemma]{lem:binomial-resolvents}
If $N\sim\mathrm{Binomial}(t,p)$ and $\kappa\ge1$, then
    \begin{equation}
    \E\sbr[3]{\frac1{\kappa+N}}
    \le\frac C{\kappa+tp},
    \qquad
    \E\sbr[3]{\frac1{(\kappa+N)^2}}
    \le\frac C{(\kappa+tp)^2}
    \end{equation}
for some absolute constant $C>0$.

