[Proposition sobolev-es of arXiv:2603.26307, '\LARGE The incompressible Navier--Stokes--Fourier system with thermal noise'] Let 
		 $(u_{\epsilon} ,\psi_{\epsilon},q_\epsilon)$ be the weak martingale solutions to  (equation ep_approx of the paper)--(equation eqn354865865 of the paper) with initial data $(u_0,\psi_0)$ constructed in Proposition (prp-existence-ep of the paper). Then there exists a constant $C= C(u_0,\psi_0, F_2,G_2,T)$, such that
		\begin{align}\begin{split}	\mathbb{E} \bigl[ \|u_\epsilon \|_{L^{7/3}([0,T]\times\mathbb{T}^3;\mathbb{R}^3)}^{7/3}\,+\,
				\| {\psi_\epsilon}\|_{L^{7/3}([0,T] \times \mathbb{T}^3)}^{7/3}
			\bigr]\,\le\, C,& \\\mathbb{E}\bigl[
		 \| u_\epsilon  \|_{L^{7/5}(0,T;W^{1,7/5}(\mathbb{T}^3;\mathbb{R}^3))}^{7/5}
				\,+\, 
			\|\psi_\epsilon \|_{L^{7/5}(0,T;W^{1,7/5}(\mathbb{T}^3))}^{7/5}\bigr]
			\,\le\, C,
			\end{split}
		\end{align}
	for any $\epsilon\in (0,1)$.

