[Proposition prop:central-tower of arXiv:2606.28869, '\bfseries A General Theory of Paths:\\ \large Signatures, Jump Lifts, and Expected Signatu'] The truncations $\pi_N:G^{(N+1)}\to G^{(N)}$ are surjective group homomorphisms with central kernel
\begin{equation}
\ker\pi_N=\exp(\mathfrak{L}_{N+1})\cong\mathbb{R}^{\ell_d(N+1)}.
\end{equation}
Hence the representation ladder
\begin{equation}
\cdots\twoheadrightarrow\mathrm{Sig}^{(N+1)}\twoheadrightarrow\mathrm{Sig}^{(N)}\twoheadrightarrow\cdots
\end{equation}
is a tower of central extensions, each step forgetting exactly the top-degree free-Lie directions, of dimension the Witt number $\ell_d(N+1)$.

[Lemma 9 of arXiv:2606.26619, 'Ergodicity of stochastic reaction-diffusion equations on unbounded domains driven by space'] Assume that (S1)--(S3) and (H5) hold. Define
  \begin{align*}
    h_{+}(u):=
  \begin{cases}
    C_{b,\theta}, & u\geq 0,\\
    -\gamma u + \sup_{u\leq v\leq 0}\big(b(v) - b(0) + C_{b,\theta}\big), & u\leq 0,
  \end{cases}
  \end{align*}
where $\gamma > 2(2\nu)^2 G_{\sigma}^2$. Let $v_{+}$ be the unique solution to equation (\ref{260603.1828}) with $\tilde{b}=h_{+}$. If
\[
m >\frac{G_{\sigma}^2}{8},
\]
then
\begin{align}
  \sup_{t\geq 0}\sup_{x\in\mathbb{R}}\mathbb{E}|v_{+}(t,x)|^2 <\infty.
\end{align}

