[Lemma 5 (Uniform fixed surplus Wright bound) of arXiv:2608.04799, '2608.04799'] For every integer \(R_0\ge0\), there is \(C=C(R_0)<\infty\) such that
\begin{equation}
  c(k,k+r-1)
  \le C k^{k+3r/2-2}
\end{equation}
for all \(k\ge1\) and \(0\le r\le R_0\), with the convention that the left
side is zero when the edge count is infeasible.

[Lem nec_hyp of arXiv:2608.30031, 'Ziggurats, taut foliations, and contact structures'] \begin{enumerate}
        \item The standard foliation by disks on $S^1 \times D^2$ cannot be $C^0$-approximated by contact structures with boundary slope $0$ for the standard boundary framing.

        \item An irrational foliation $\mathcal{F}$ on $\mathbb{T}^2 \times I$ cannot be $C^0$-approximated by contact structures realizing the same boundary slopes as $\mathcal{F}$. 
    \end{enumerate}

[Theorem LSL^2 of arXiv:2605.10309, 'Exponential Decay of $L^2$-Solutions to Stochastic Nonlinear Schr\"odinger Equations Drive'] Assume (H1) and (H2), and let $1<\alpha <1+\frac{4}{d}$.
Then for any $x\in L^2$ and $0<T<\infty$, there exists a sequence of $L^2$-solutions $(y_n,\tau_n), n\in\mathbb{N}$ of (equation RSNLS2 of the paper) where $(\tau_n)_{n\in\mathbb{N}}$ is a sequence of increasing stopping times.
For every $n\ge 1$, it holds ${
{\mathbf{P}}\text{-a.s.}}$ that
\begin{align}
y_n|_{[0,\tau_n]}\in C([0,\tau_n];L^2)\cap L^{q}(0,\tau_n;L^{\alpha+1}),
\end{align}
and uniqueness holds in $C([0,\tau_n];L^2)\cap L^{q}(0,\tau_n;L^{\alpha+1})$. Here, $(q,\alpha+1)$ is a Strichartz pair, where $q=\frac{4(\alpha+1)}{d(\alpha-1)}\in (2+\frac{4}{d},\infty).$
Moreover, defining $\displaystyle \tau^*(x)=\lim_{n\to\infty}\tau_n$ and $\displaystyle y=\lim_{n\to\infty}y_n\mathbf{1}_{[0,\tau^*(x))}$, we have the blowup alternative, that is, for ${
{\mathbf{P}}\text{-a.s.}} \ \omega$, if $\tau^*(x)(\omega)<T$, then
\[ \lim_{t\to \tau^*(x)(\omega)}\|y(t)(\omega)\|_{L^2}=\infty. \]

