[Lem estimate of arXiv:2503.22334, 'Probabilistic analysis of optimal multi-pivot QuickSort'] For all $0 \le L<\infty$ exists an $M_L<\infty$ such that for all $\lambda \in [-L,L]$ and all $n \ge 0$ we have
    \begin{align}
        \E{e^{\lambda X_n}} \le e^{\lambda^2 M_L}.
    \end{align}

