body:
[Definition 8 of arXiv:2607.07283, 'Multi-time Markov renewal chains and stratified renewal theorems'] The Markov renewal potential associated with $q$ is the kernel sequence $\psi$ defined by

\begin{equation*}
\psi_k(x,A)=\sum_{n\geq0}q^{(n)}_k(x,A).
\end{equation*}

When $q$ is strict, this sum is finite for each fixed $k$. In general it is interpreted as a non-negative kernel, possibly sigma-finite.

[Prop propbasicproperty of arXiv:2608.29914, 'Fixed points in abstract provability structures'] Let $S = \langle L, \leq, \top, \bot, \Box, \boxtimes\rangle$ be an APS.
Then, the following statements hold: 
    \begin{enumerate}
        \item $\top = \boxtimes \bot = \Box \top$.

        \item For every $x \in L$, we have $\boxtimes \top \leq \boxtimes x \leq \Box^k \boxtimes x \leq \Box^{k+1} \boxtimes x$ for all $k \geq 0$. 
    \end{enumerate}

