body:
[Cor 40 of arXiv:2605.23308, 'Convergence rate estimates for semigroups and heat kernels associated with resistance form'] Suppose that $(F_n,R_n,\mu_n,\rho_n)\in\bbF_r$ converges to $(F,R,\mu,\rho)\in\bbF$ in the Gromov-Hausdorff-vague topology.
Then there exists a constant $\g{c}{1_1.1}\in (0,\infty)$ such that 
\begin{align}
  \sup_{\substack{n\in\N\\x\in F_n}}\|g^{\alpha,n}(x,\cdot)\|_{\Lip^1}\vee \sup_{x\in F}\|g^{\alpha}(x,\cdot)\|_{\Lip^1}\lesssim \g{c}{1_1.1} \left(1+\frac{1}{\alpha}\right),\quad \alpha\in (0,\infty),
\end{align} 
where $g^{\alpha,n}$ is the $\alpha$-potential density associated with $(F_n,R_n,\mu_n)$. (Proof in the paper; no proof environment follows the statement in the TeX.)

