[Definition def:pointwise of arXiv:2608.11931, '\texorpdfstring{Nonlinear parabolic characterizations of stochastic completeness at infini'] Let $T>0$ and $u_0 \colon X\to\mathbb R$.  A \emph{pointwise solution of the (eq:GPME of the paper)
on $[0,T]\times X$ with initial datum $u_0$}
is a function $u \colon [0,T]\times X\to\mathbb R$ such that
\begin{enumerate}[label=(\alph*)]
    \item[\textup{(a)}] $u(t,\cdot)\in\mathcal{F}_\Phi$ for every $t\in(0,T)$;
    \item[\textup{(b)}] $u(\cdot,x)\in C([0,T])\cap C^1((0,T))$ for every $x\in X$;
    \item[\textup{(c)}] $(\partial_t +\Delta\Phi)u(t,x)=0$ for every $(t,x)\in(0,T)\times X$;
    \item[\textup{(d)}] $u(0,x)=u_0(x)$ for every $x\in X$.
\end{enumerate}
The solution $u$ is a \emph{bounded pointwise solution} if $u$ is bounded.

[Theorem th:Schauder_est of arXiv:2608.30493, '\bf McKean-Vlasov Differential Equations:\\ {An introduction and a focus on some kinetic m'] For any $\alpha,\gamma\geq 0 $ and $T>0$, there exists $C=C(\alpha,\gamma,T,B)>0$ such that 
\begin{equation}
\|\mathscr{P}_r \varphi\|_{B,\gamma+\alpha} + \|\mathscr{P}'_r \varphi\|_{B,\gamma+\alpha} \leq C\, r^{-\frac{\alpha}{2}} \|\varphi\|_{B,\gamma}, \qquad    r\in (0,T], 
\end{equation}
for any $\varphi\in C^{b}(\mathbb{R}^d)$. (Proof in the paper; no proof environment follows the statement in the TeX.)

