[Proposition prop:borel-trace-form-event of arXiv:2608.02459, 'Response Calculus for Spectral Simplicity\\ and Joint Eigenvalue Densities'] There exists a Borel set $\Omega_{\rm tr}\subseteq\Omega_{\rm GMC}$ with
$\mathbb P(\Omega_{\rm tr})=1$ such that the conclusions of
Lemma~(lem:rough-domain-full-quasi-support of the paper) hold for every
$x\in\Omega_{\rm tr}$, with $M_h$ replaced by $M_x$.  For each such $x$, the
killed Brownian motion time-changed by $M_x$ is associated on $L^2(M_x)$ with
the closed, densely defined Dirichlet form $(\mathcal E,V_x)$, where
\begin{equation}
 \begin{aligned}
  \mathcal E(u,v)&=\frac1{2\pi}\int_D\nabla u\cdot\nabla v\,dz,
  \qquad u,v\inV_x,\\
  V_x&=\{u\in H_0^1(D):\widetilde u\in L^2(M_x)\}.
 \end{aligned}
\end{equation}

