[Definition of arXiv:2604.17253, 'Large Deviations for the Nonlinear Schrödinger Equation with Randomized Quasi-Periodic Ini'] The {\em second counting function} $\ell$ is defined by
\begin{align*}
\ell(\gamma^{(k)})=
\begin{cases}
0, & \gamma^{(k)}=0, \ k\ge1; \\
1, & \gamma^{(1)}=1; \\
1+\sum_{j=1}^{3}\ell(\gamma_j^{(k-1)}), & \gamma^{(k)}=(\gamma_j^{(k-1)})_{j=1}^3,\ k\ge2.
\end{cases}
\end{align*}

[Lemma 21 of arXiv:2604.18871, 'Quantitative approximation of the Vlasov(--Fokker--Planck)--Navier--Stokes system by stoch'] There exists $C \equiv C(T,k,A,\lVert u \rVert_{L^\infty_{x}}, \gamma, d,p)>0$ such that for any $N\in \N^*$,
\begin{align*}
\big\| u_t^{(N)} - u_t \big\|_{ \gamma,p}
\leq C \int_{0}^t \frac{1}{(t-s)^{\tilde{\gamma}}} \Big( \big\| u_s^{(N)} - u_s \big\|_{ \gamma,p} +  \big\| \langle v \rangle^{k} (F^{(N)}_{s}-F_{s}) \big\|_{L^{2}_{x,v}} \Big) \dd s ,
\end{align*}
where $\tilde{\gamma}\in (0,1)$ is defined in \eqref{eq:deftildegamma}.

