body:
[Lem 15 of arXiv:2609.03869, '\bf Sharp asymptotics for a transport model with a nonlocal condition of the Fisher-KPP ty'] Let $u$ be the bounded and continuous solution of the linear transport problem
	\eqref{moving frame-u} associated with an absolutely continuous, bounded and compactly supported  initial datum
	$u_0$ in $[0,i^\dagger)\times\mathbb R$. 
	Then, for every $T>0$ and $\boldsymbol{a}>0$,
	\begin{equation}

	|u(t,0,x)|\le C_{\boldsymbol{a},T}e^{-\boldsymbol{a} x}~~~~~\text{for all}~~(t,x)\in [0,T]\times\R,
	\end{equation}
	with $C_{\boldsymbol{a},T}:=
		\mathscr{R}_0\K_{\boldsymbol{a}} M_{u_0}
	e^{
		\K_{\boldsymbol{a}}
		\S_0\tau_\infty T}$, where $\K_{\boldsymbol{a}}:=
		\int_{\mathbb R}
		\K_*(x)e^{\boldsymbol{a} x}\md x$ and $M_{u_0}:=
		\max_{(i,x)\in[0,i_\dagger)\times\R}
		e^{\boldsymbol{a} x}|u_0(i,x)|.$

