[Lemma 43 of arXiv:2511.10535, 'Eigenvalues of Brownian Motions on $\mathrm{GL}(N,\mathbb{C})$'] Let $B_0^N$ be a deterministic matrix. There exists a constant $C_{\rho,t}$ such that, for any $y\in\R$, we have that
    \begin{align*}
        &\left| \E\left[\ts_N\left(e^{\i y \left|B^N_0B^N(t)-z\right|^2}\right)\right] - \tau_N\left(e^{\i y |B^N_0b(t)-z|^2}\right) \right| \\
        & \leq C_{\rho,t} \frac{(1+y^4)(1+|z|^4)(1+\norm{B^N_0}^4)}{N^2},
    \end{align*}
    where we used the construction of the space $\A_N$ of Lemma \ref{lem:bigspace} to define the product of $B^N_0$ and $b(t)$.

