{"artifact_digest":"sha256:402f4550fb981998325cf02f6a945d949bce220873cf6c34870f52097a164ac3","artifact_path":"objects/sha256/40/402f4550fb981998325cf02f6a945d949bce220873cf6c34870f52097a164ac3.md","bundle_digest":"sha256:d40e723ba4f91162d13ebab86f4dac24bf7afa185cd96d328c324f21c8b2a0d6","bundle_entry_key":"2608-30357-lemma-4-existence-integral","bundle_id":"population.tex-extract-s3_127","claim_kind":"lemma","conditions":[],"domain":"probability theory","draft":"tex-extract-20260907/bundle_s3_127.json","evidence_ids":[],"logical_id":"math:harvest.arxiv.mathematics:arxiv-2608-30357-lemm-4-existence-integral","overlay_schema_version":1,"proof_text":"Paper's own proof, opening: We only give the proof for the CUI condition, the argument for  UI is analogous. Due to \eqref{eq:CUI-condition}, there exists $n_0 \in \bN$ such that for all $n \ge n_0$,
	\begin{align*}
		\bE\int_{S_n} \lt\|X^n_s\rt\|^p \1_{\{X^n_s \notin K_n\}} \nu_n(\od s) \le 1.
	\end{align*}
Then, for $n \ge n_0$, one has
\begin{align*}
	\bE\int_{S_n} \lt\|X^n_s\rt\|^p  \nu_n(\od s)  & = \bE\int_{S_n} \lt\|X^n_s\rt\|^p \1_{\{X^n_s \in K_n\}} \nu_n(\od s) + \bE\int_{S_n} \lt\|X^n_s\rt\|^p \1_{\{X^n_s \notin K_n\}} \nu_n(\od s) \\
	& \le \|K_n\|^p \nu_n(S_n) + 1 \le \lt\|K_n\rt\|^p C_\nu + 1 <\infty.
\end{align*}
