[Theorem thm:stable-four-dimensional-restated of arXiv:2608.23135, 'Graph distance and effective resistance of the random walk trace in four and five dimensio'] Recall that $b_X$ is the constant in (equation Eq2 of the paper). Then
\[
\frac{
X_n-\mathbb{E}[X_n]
-\frac{b_X}{2}n(\log n)^{-3/2}\log\log n
}{
n(\log n)^{-3/2}
}
\Rightarrow
Z_{4,X},
\]
where $Z_{4,X}$ is a non-degenerate stable random variable of index $1$ with
skewness $-1$.

