[Corollary cor:OZ of arXiv:2605.15545, 'Crossover from subcritical to critical decay: \\ random walk, self-avoiding walk, percolat'] [Ornstein--Zernike decay]

Let $d\ge 1$ and
suppose that Assumptions~(ass:Omega of the paper) and~(ass:J of the paper) hold.
For nonzero $x \in {\mathbb Z^d}$, let ${\mu_{\hat x}},\eta_{\hat x},\Lambda_{\hat x}$ be given by Proposition~(prop:geom-intro of the paper).
Then as $\abs x\to \infty$, we have
\begin{equation}
S(x) =
	\frac 1 { (2\pi)^{(d-1)/2} \sqrt{\det\Lambda_{\hat x}} }
	\frac{1}{ (\hat x \cdot \Lambda_{\hat x}^{-1} \hat x)^{1/2} }
	\frac{ \norm {\eta_{\hat x}}_2^{(d-3)/2}} { \norm  x_2^{(d-1)/2}}
	e^{-m_S  \abs x_S}
	[ \hat h ^{(\mu_{\hat x})} (0) + o(1)] ,
\end{equation}
with the $o(1)$ depending only on $d,M,K_{\mathrm{IR}},\zeta,m_S$. (Proof in the paper; no proof environment follows the statement in the TeX.)

[Corollary cor:bw of arXiv:2607.06249, 'Extreme least singular values of Gaussian row submatrices and a phase retrieval stability '] Let $A_m\in\mathbb{R}^{(2m-1)\times m}$ have independent standard Gaussian entries. Then
\begin{equation}
  \frac{1}{m}\log\omega(A_m)\xrightarrow{P}-\log4,
\end{equation}
with the rate
\begin{equation}
  \mathbb{P}\left\{\left|\frac{1}{m}\log\omega(A_m)+\log4\right|>\varepsilon\right\}=O_\varepsilon(m^{-1})
\end{equation}
for every fixed $\varepsilon>0$. Equivalently, $\omega(A_m)=4^{-m+o_P(m)}$.

Let $R_m=\max_{1\le i\le 2m-1}\|a_i\|$. For every $b>1/4$, $\mathbb{P}\{\omega(A_m)\le R_m b^m\}\to1$. For
every $b<1/4$ and every fixed $C<\infty$, $\mathbb{P}\{\omega(A_m)\le C R_m b^m\}\to0$. Thus the Gaussian
critical base in the Balan--Wang question is $1/4$. (Proof in the paper; no proof environment follows the statement in the TeX.)

