[Lemma 2 of arXiv:2604.25336, 'Central limit theorem for slow-fast system under mixed fractional Brownian motion'] (\cite[Lemma 3.10]{Hairer-Li})Let \(p\ge 2\) and \(\alpha>\frac{1}{2}\). Assume that \(x_{\cdot}\in \mathcal{B}_{\alpha,p}\), let \(f\in \mathcal{C}^{-\kappa,\gamma}\)(deterministic) for some \(\kappa, \gamma\) such that \(\eta=H-\kappa>\frac{1}{2}\) and \(\bar \eta=H-\kappa+\gamma\alpha\) and define
$A_{s,t}:=\int_{s}^{t}f(r, x_s)d B_{r}^H$ where the integral is defined as a conditional Wiener integral. Then \(A\in H_\eta^p\cap \bar H_{\bar \eta}^p\) and 
\begin{equation}
\|\int_{s}^{t}f(r, x_r)d B_{r}^H\|_{p} \lesssim |f|_{-\kappa,p}(|t-s|^{H-\kappa}+\|x\|_{\alpha}(t-s)^{(\bar \eta -\alpha)})
\end{equation}
and 
\begin{equation}
\|\mathbb{E}\big(\int_{s}^{t}(f(r, x_r)-f(r, x_s))d B_{r}^H|\mathcal{F}_s\big)\|_{p} \lesssim |f|_{-\kappa,p}\|x\|_{\alpha}(t-s)^{(\bar \eta -\alpha)}.
\end{equation} (Proof in the paper; no proof environment follows the statement in the TeX.)

[Theorem 27 (Krawtchouk mass concentration) of arXiv:2609.03736, '2609.03736'] For every fixed $c<\delta_\pi$, there are $C_c,\gamma_c>0$ such that every
$g\in\cE_n^+\cup\cE_n^-$ satisfies
\begin{equation}
 \sum_{0\leq i<\lceil cn\rceil}w_i|g_i|
 \leq C_ce^{-\gamma_cn}\sum_{i=0}^nw_i|g_i|.

\end{equation}

[Lemma lem:process_continuity of arXiv:2606.11951, 'On Skorokhod Problems for Reflected and Singular Stochastic Heat Equations'] The process $X^a$ is almost surely continuous in the sense that
	\begin{equation*}
		\mathbb{P}_z[X_t^a \in [C_0] \text{ for a.e. } t\in [0,\infty)] = 1 \quad\text{for all } z\inL.
	\end{equation*}
	The same statement holds for $\mathcal{E}$-q.e.\ $z\inL$ for $X$.

