Let U be an open set in R^d and let {K_n} be a sequence of precompact open sets exhausting U with closure(K_n) subset K_{n+1}. Let X_t^n be the unique global strong solution of an SDE with coefficients agreeing with mu, sigma on K_n. Define tau_n = inf{t >= 0 : X_t^n not in K_n}. Then for m > n, X_t^m = X_t^n on [0, tau_n] almost surely, and X_t := X_t^n for t <= tau_n defines a unique local strong solution on [0, tau_infinity) with tau_infinity = lim_{n -> infinity} tau_n.
Pathwise uniqueness holds for truncated Lipschitz systems
Compact exhaustion {K_n}

[Proposition 27 of arXiv:2608.02927, 'Thinning Operation via the Poisson-F\"ollmer Process'] [Variational formula for entropy] 

      Let $(\Omega, \mathcal{F},\mu)$ be a probability space, and let $f : \Omega \rightarrow (0,\infty) $ be a $\mu$--integrable function such that $\int_{\Omega} f \dd \mu = 1.$ Then 
      \begin{displaymath}
          \Ent_{ \mu } (f) = \sup_{g} \Big\{ \int f g \dd \mu - \log \Big( \int e^{g} \dd \mu \Big) \Big\}
      \end{displaymath}
      where the supremum is taken over measurable and bounded functions $g : \Omega \rightarrow \R.$ (Proof in the paper; no proof environment follows the statement in the TeX.)

[Proposition prop:harmonic-grad of arXiv:2609.02987, 'Tail Likelihood Reinforcement Learning'] Under (lem:tailrl-regularity of the paper), for every $T\geq1$,
\begin{equation}
\nabla_\theta J_{\mathrm{TailRL{}}}^{(T)}(\theta;x)
=
\sum_{k=1}^{T}
\frac{1}{k}
\nabla_\theta\text{Best-of-}k(\theta;x).

\end{equation}
Equivalently,
\begin{equation}
\nabla_\theta J_{\mathrm{TailRL{}}}^{(T)}(\theta;x)
=
\int_0^1
\frac{1-\left(1-p_\theta(x,\tau)\right)^T}
{p_\theta(x,\tau)}
\nabla_\theta p_\theta(x,\tau)
\,d\tau,

\end{equation}
where the ratio is interpreted by continuity as $T$ when $p_\theta(x,\tau)=0$.

