{"artifact_digest":"sha256:531a71c291a158e4a94b7e3fb6937fd6b80b81654739496be121a92daf4949c4","artifact_path":"objects/sha256/53/531a71c291a158e4a94b7e3fb6937fd6b80b81654739496be121a92daf4949c4.md","bundle_digest":"sha256:7ecd18934c63ce80bc2b16347d2db8022d1360ae774c002499199b253d08d7f8","bundle_entry_key":"2604-12334-theorem-12-prop-12","bundle_id":"population.tex-extract-s3_012","claim_kind":"theorem","conditions":[],"domain":"probability theory","draft":"tex-extract-20260907/bundle_s3_012.json","evidence_ids":[],"logical_id":"math:harvest.arxiv.mathematics:arxiv-2604-12334-prop-12-prop-12","overlay_schema_version":1,"proof_text":"Paper's own proof, opening: Recall the definition of $g(S)$ given in \eqref{eq: g(S)}. Then 
    \begin{align*}
        g(S) &= \frac{1}{\pi(S) \pi(S')} \sum_{\substack{x \in S \\ y \in S'}} \pi(x) P(x,y)\\
        &= \frac{1}{\pi(S)}  \sum_{\substack{x \in S \\ y \in S'}} \pi(x) P(x,y) + \frac{1}{\pi(S')} \sum_{\substack{x \in S \\ y \in S'}} \pi(x) P(x,y).\\
    \end{align*}
    By $\pi$-reversibility of $P$, the first term yields
    \begin{align*}
        \frac{1}{\pi(S)}  \sum_{\substack{x \in S \\ y \in S'}} \pi(x) P(x,y) &= \frac{1}{\pi(S)}  \sum_{\substack{x \in S' \\ y \in S}} \pi(x) P(x,y)\\
        &= \frac{1}{\pi(S)} \sum_{x\in S'} \pi(x) \left[1 - \sum_{y \in S'}P(x,y)\right]\\
        &= ...","release_manifest_digest":"sha256:d964f1cdd34feb1824769633f84687fa640dd74f9bd46bc7e7461741d1fe5c9a","revision_digest":"sha256:f9a6aa0f227ce552314a8b570918bcb8083c27983bb287986185cf3abd78074a","source_id":"arxiv:2604.12334","source_revision":"tex-as-downloaded-2026-09-07","statement_fidelity_reviewed":false,"supersedes":[],"trust_class":"curated_secondary","truth_status":"unverified"}

