[Theorem 2 of arXiv:2506.18063, 'Reduced critical branching processes in non-favorable random environment \thanks{ This wor'] Assume that Conditions $B1$ and $B2$ are valid. If $
k\sim \theta m=\theta m(n)\rightarrow \infty $ as $n\rightarrow \infty $ in
such a way that $m=o(n)$, then, for any $y\geq 0$ and $t>0$
\begin{equation}
\lim_{n\gg k\rightarrow \infty }\mathbf{P}\left( \log Z_{r,n}\leq ya_{m}|
\mathcal{R}\left( ta_{k},n\right) \right) =A(\theta ^{1/\alpha }t,\theta
^{1/\alpha }\left( t\wedge y\right) ),  
\end{equation}
where
\begin{equation*}
A(T,y)=\frac{\alpha \rho +1}{T^{1+\alpha \rho }}\int_{0}^{\infty }w^{\alpha
\rho }\mathbf{P}\left( -w\leq \min_{0\leq s\leq 1}Y_{s}\leq y-w;Y_{1}\leq
T-w\right) dw
\end{equation*}
for $y\in \lbrack 0,T].$ (Proof in the paper; no proof environment follows the statement in the TeX.)

[Prop thin-chaos of arXiv:2602.06011, 'Excursion decomposition of the XOR-Ising model'] Let $\alpha\in(0,1)$. For any $a<a_c(\alpha)$, let $\mathds A_{-a,a}$ be a subcritical two-valued set in a valid domain $D$. For any continuous, bounded  function $f:\mathbb C\to\mathbb R$, 
    \begin{align}
    \lim_{n\to \infty} (\field{e^{i\alpha \phi}}, f\1_{[\mathds A_{-a, a}]_n}) =0, 
    \end{align}
    where the limit is in probability.

